   "**A Super El Niño is the multiplier; land clearing is the cause** — the direct effect of drought is that peat that would have stayed wet burns; the compound consequence is that attributing the fires to the weather converts a land-use decision into a natural disaster, so the same concession holders are protected by the same alibi in the next dry year, and the one after",
   "**The haze is a foreign-policy problem ASEAN has no instrument for** — the direct effect is diplomatic notes from Singapore, Malaysia and the Philippines; the compound consequence is that no enforcement mechanism exists because the fires are lit on land whose ownership is opaque, and the one dataset that would make enforcement possible — which company holds which concession — is the dataset that is not published",
   "**Protests are the hinge being tested early** — the direct effect is that the fires have become a domestic political question rather than a seasonal emergency; the compound consequence is that if the answer is water-bombing and face masks without land-title disclosure and peat rewetting, the grievance returns next year with a larger crowd and a bigger number, and the state will have spent its credibility on spraying",
