  "hinge": "The cause is not the flaw — flaws are ordinary. It is the choice — by the foundations and companies that maintain shared code, whether the language under a third of the web is staffed and audited as a public utility or left to volunteers; by governments, whether a public-facing service carries a patch deadline with an audit attached rather than an advisory; by the AI labs, whether discovery capability is released under a protocol that gives defenders a head start; and by every small organisation still running its own server, whether \"temporarily down for maintenance\" is a strategy or a warning it has not read. §12 is not a promise of punishment; it is a statement about how hidden things behave — a flaw, like a lie, is discovered in its own time, and the only variable is who discovers it first. Whether the next decade of the web is built on audited, funded foundations or on a stack of unowned code that an AI happens to find before a criminal does, is not fixed by the technology; it is a decision held by named foundations, named agencies and named companies, and one that a different choice could still make."
